{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal would result in the loss of a&nbsp;family sized dwellinghouse. It is therefore at odds with the above policies which seek to protect family sized housing, for which there is demonstrable need in the borough. It further does not appear to address an identified need, with no information submitted in this regard. It is therefore considered contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (December 2023)Policy SP3 and DMH5 of the LBBD Local Plan (September 2024",
    "The proposed HMO has the potential to increase activity level and coming and goings to and from the site leading to additional levels of noise and disturbance at the property and fails to present adeqaute waste storage capacity. This is considered to have a negative impact on neighbouring amenity in this street of family housing and in turn the health and wellbeing of neighbouring residents.&nbsp; As such the proposal is contrary to the following:Policies SP7, DMD1, DMSI3 and DMSI8 of the LBBD Local Plan (September 2024)The Council&#39;s Planning Advice Note on Waste and Recycling Provisions in New and Refurbished Residential Developments",
    "The proposal fails to demonstrate that adequate cycle storage could be provided on the site which is well-located and of sufficient size. As such, the proposal is contrary to:Policy T5 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMT3&nbsp;&nbsp;of the LBBD Local Plan (September 2024)London Cycling Design Standards (2016)"
  ],
